es to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","assistance":"AI-assisted architectural interpretation and procedural recipe authoring; deterministic Python/Blender export. No photographic textures.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["The saved OSM footprint and 47 height-tagged parts define the 60 m pyramidal bell tower, 26.8 m nave/apse, low aisles, chapels and buttresses. Many chapel heights carry IGN Lidar HD provenance; original roof directions and heights are retained.","One 10.5 square metre mapped part has no height; it remains represented only by the common foundation rather than inventing a volume. Hidden internal part intersections are not a watertight building interior.","Inspected eligible references 00,03,06 confirm the tall square Romanesque tower with paired rounded bell bays, steep slate spire, long nave clerestory and attached lower street-front buildings. Bell windows, nave rhythm, stone ledges and clock are schematic map-scale inferences.","Skillion roofs include hidden stone undersides to make their volume closed and normal orientation unambiguous; no exposed sloped roofs face downward. Window and bell-bay panels use the shared light-blue window material and are clipped to actual constructed walls. Fine louvres, sculpture, clock ornament, roof crosses and individual masonry are omitted. Grey roof material substitutes for the photographed slate color."],"source":{"url":"/assets/saint-germain-des-pres/a40a92d6becac9d478f4ab7de0e5218a7460f72ba64eac79c604e1c2d04fec0e/source.blend.gz","bytes":146850,"sha256":"5bf9cde359c203a82469f74f72450a0655a2621184596893c6e712869a255c47"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/assets/saint-germain-des-pres/a40a92d6becac9d478f4ab7de0e5218a7460f72ba64eac79c604e1c2d04fec0e/spatial-source.json","bytes":38509,"sha256":"62f6a00563238b5fa2fae2fa346ca1c33a13c640638eb5b81cab6780df5c2056"},"preview":{"url":"/as